From bc0f08be05733c48577cbcfe6454f6cebe579503 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude (Cowork)" <silvagni.dario@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 12:55:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add Griglia variant to Media block; render videos wherever
 referenced
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- New "grid" variant on the Media block (blocks/media.ts): an array of
  video+poster+caption items (1-12), for laying out many reels at once
  instead of one full-bleed section per video.
- media-block.tsx: renders the grid as a responsive page-grid — 3
  columns desktop, 2 tablet, 1 mobile — each cell a 9:16 video loop.
- MediaImage now detects a video mime type and renders a muted, looping
  <video> instead of handing the URL to next/image. Previously any
  video referenced outside the Loop video variant (Hero Media, Coppia
  affiancata, Full bleed, Prima/dopo) rendered a broken-image icon with
  only the alt text visible, since next/image cannot decode a video
  stream. This was affecting a real project already in the CMS.
